From c10ac6974a54617272be1e9dce1e804a168f8b1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <moises.santana@ifba.edu.br>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:35:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/36] feat: per-boot-ROM-revision CGB post-boot DIV via
 --model cgb0|cgb-abcde

Mooneye boot_div-cgb0 and boot_div-cgbABCDE are mutually exclusive on
real hardware (pass: CGB 0 vs pass: CGB ABCDE): the boot-ROM families
leave the DIV counter at different values/phases at handoff. One fixed
configured constant can satisfy only one of them.

- GBConfig gains GBCGBRevision cgb_revision (default revision 0, so
  existing behavior and every currently passing test are unchanged)
- DMG-compat post-boot div_counter: 0x2884 (revision 0) or 0x2678
  (revisions A-E), matching the MTS-verified read sequences
  29 2A 2A 2B 2C 2E / 27 28 28 29 2A 2C
- generated main accepts --model cgb0 (explicit revision-0 pin) and
  --model cgb-abcde; cgb/auto keep revision 0
- RUNTIME.md documents the new model values
- Crystal contract runtime_tree_sha256 refreshed (bd11c468...)

Evidence: mooneye suite 75/75 after the runner pins each test (next
commit); ctest 84/85 (remaining failure is pre-existing); generated
smoke builds fresh from this tree.
