Fast forward, save state, load state, state slot, mute and the debug overlay all
changed state with no feedback at all. Slot changes already built a status
string, but it only rendered inside the settings menu, which you have to open
to read.

Adds a bottom-right toast, 1.5 s, hard cut, one message at a time:

  FAST FORWARD    ON / OFF      MAX SPEED       ON / OFF
  STATE SAVED     SLOT 2        STATE LOADED    SLOT 2
  STATE SLOT      3             SOUND           OFF / ON
  DEBUG OVERLAY   ON / OFF      and SAVE/LOAD FAILED, DELETE FAILED, SLOT DELETED

Three decisions worth naming.

The toast is a sibling `if`, not one more `else if` in the chain that draws the
menu and the debug overlay. Those two are mutually exclusive today, so a toast
in that chain would disappear every time the player opened the menu - which is
exactly when they are most likely to have just pressed something and want to
see that it took.

Fast forward is confirmed on both edges. It is a hold action rather than a
toggle, and it is assigned outside the action switch where the controller path
also flows through, so a per-frame edge check there fires the toast once on
press and once on release instead of on every frame of the hold.

Savestate toasts are fired from inside set_savestate_status() rather than from
the switch, because save, load and delete all funnel through it, and so do the
menu buttons. One call site covers every path. The `detail` argument is
deliberately left out of the toast: it is usually a full path and does not
belong in a one-line message, but the menu still shows it.

Drawn by ImGui on top of the game texture and never into the guest framebuffer,
which is what keeps the oracle meaningful here. Measured, not assumed: frame
dumps at frames 400, 700, 1000, 1100 and 1200 are byte-identical between a
build from before this change and a build from after it, and the gates are
unchanged - 75/75, SameBoy 3 EXACT + 2 NEAR 0.004, PyBoy 5/5 EXACT.

No inputs, no focus, no nav on the window, and no queue: holding a toggle key
must not stack twenty messages. RPCS3 has an open request to disable its own
"Screenshot Saved" overlay for exactly this reason, so the bar here is that the
player should be able to forget it is there.
