From e613498bcffc803e63900fb4ee5ac63610e1f899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <191926848+msantana-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:01:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/36] platform: name the host after the cartridge and give
 the menu some shape

Two problems with the settings screen, one of them wrong on any ROM.

The window and the menu both opened as "GameBoy Recompiled", which is the
upstream engine's own product name. This executable takes whatever ROM the
user supplies, so every game was being labelled with the name of the toolchain
that translated it. gb_context_get_rom_title() already existed and was only
being used to name the save file; it is now exported as gbrt_get_rom_title()
and reads the cartridge header at 0x134, so a build started from any ROM labels
itself with that game. Exposed rather than duplicated on purpose: the parsing
has a fallback path for a missing or too-short ROM, and two copies of that
would drift.

Then the layout. On a 4K window every control spanned the whole screen - a
1900 px wide "Speed %" slider - and because most widgets carry their label as
their last argument, that label ended up stranded against the far edge, metres
from the control it named. The content is now bounded and centred, which pulls
each label back beside its control without touching any individual widget. A
first pass at hierarchy: sections were Separator() + TextDisabled(), the same
weight as every control under them, so fifteen sections had no shape at all.
They now get a rule, air and the accent colour. The bitmap font is not scaled,
because scaling a bitmap font only blurs it.

Palette moves off Dear ImGui's default blue, which reads as an unfinished
demo, to the greens of a DMG palette plus a near-black, so the widgets sit in
the same family as the hardware and as the toast.

Not done, and deliberately: the Controls section is still a wall of near
identical rows, and the audio device diagnostics are still dumped raw into the
settings flow as though they were configuration. Both want another pass with
a screenshot in the loop, which is not something this change could settle on
its own.

Verified rather than assumed. Frame dumps at 400, 700, 1000, 1100 and 1200 are
byte-identical against a build from before this and before the toast, because
none of this reaches the guest framebuffer. Gates unchanged: 75/75, SameBoy
3 EXACT + 2 NEAR 0.004, PyBoy 5/5 EXACT. No line in the diff touches
render_frame_internal, the texture upload, or the PPU.
