From b55ab9cd91655bfc916556e191885105f1688558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <191926848+msantana-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:16:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/36] platform: move Resume to the footer and fix the header
 alignment on wide screens

Caught on a 4K display. "Resume" sat in the header positioned by a SameLine()
offset measured from the start of the line, which is right only on a narrow
window. ImGui resets the cursor X to the line start after every item, so on a
4K screen content_x is far from the left padding and the button drifted away
from the column it belonged to. The subtitle was sliding out to the far left
for the same reason and had been invisible until now, because on a 936 px
window content_x coincides with the padding and the whole header happened to
line up.

Resume moves to the footer, between Reset Display and Quit, which is where it
was always meant to be: the footer is already the action row, and equal-width
buttons there need no position arithmetic. Every header line now sets its own
cursor X rather than assuming SetCursorPosX persists.

The footer also used to measure the full window width, putting Reset Display
against the far left and Quit against the far right while everything between
them sat in a centred 900 px column. It is bounded to the same column now.

Verified the way a UI-only change can actually be verified: it compiles, and
the guest framebuffer is byte-identical at frames 400, 700, 1000, 1100 and
1200 against a build from before any of this. The emulation gates were
deliberately not re-run here - they measure accuracy, this change touches none
of it, and running them per commit would train everyone to skip reading the
result. They belong before the public release, where the recorded baseline has
to stand behind a published pin.
