From b0ed464c7b81a08c02738c8b9a05742afdb36a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <191926848+msantana-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:20:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/36] platform: centre the footer buttons on the content
 column

Caught on screen: Reset Display, Resume and Quit were pinned to the left edge
while everything above them sat in a centred column.

This is the exact mistake the previous commit described and then made again.
SetCursorPosX only holds for the next item, and it had been placed before the
Separator; submitting the Separator put the cursor back at the line start, so
the first button landed at zero. It now sits immediately before the button.

Audited every other SetCursorPosX(content_x) in the menu: each one is
immediately followed by the item it positions, so the header is the only place
this bit and it is correct.

Compiles, and the guest framebuffer stays byte-identical at frames 400, 700,
1000, 1100 and 1200 against a build from before any of the UI work. Not
visible to me - there is no way to screenshot the menu from here - so this is
reasoned from the ImGui semantics, not observed.
