From be167df0313fe38048668cd52aa751f308baaf02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <191926848+msantana-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:18:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/36] runtime: include math.h for the panel effects

fmaxf, lrintf, fabsf and expf were reaching the compiler only because GCC 14
pulls <math.h> in transitively on this host. GCC 11 through the MinGW headers
does not, so the file does not compile for a Windows cross build. The include is
what was always required; only its absence was accidental.

Found by cross-compiling for Windows, which is the first thing to build this
file with a toolchain older than the one it was developed against.
---
 runtime/src/platform_sdl.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runtime/src/platform_sdl.cpp b/runtime/src/platform_sdl.cpp
index 033bf79..7ff35ca 100644
--- a/runtime/src/platform_sdl.cpp
+++ b/runtime/src/platform_sdl.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,10 @@
 #include <cctype>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
+// fmaxf/lrintf/fabsf/expf. Not transitive on every toolchain: the panel effects
+// reached GCC 11 through the MinGW headers only because this was missing and
+// GCC 14 happened to pull it in here.
+#include <math.h>
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <string>
 #if defined(_WIN32)
