From 92a1ea86c885daf10a16241d0829e15aed20c950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <moises.santana@ifba.edu.br>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:09:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/36] presentation: export LCDC per scanline and raise the
 ABI to 2

The hardware snapshot carried only the end-of-frame LCDC, which cannot see a
row the guest assembled from another background map: Ghost Babel selects the
second map for its bottom HUD band and restores the register at vblank, so the
band's rows are invisible to a frontend that reads the register once per frame.

The PPU records LCDC at the start of each visible scanline's dot transfer,
which is the value that row draws with (the live register, not the latch), and
the presentation ABI exports the 144-byte record.

The record lives in GBContext rather than in GBPPU on purpose: the savestate
serializes the PPU struct and validates its size, so a field there would make
every state written before it unreadable. Per-frame telemetry has no business
invalidating saved games.
---
