From dca9cf12c39fe2d8b9288b95a0c77245a874cdba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <moises.santana@ifba.edu.br>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:45:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/36] tests: cover the per-scanline LCDC record

The ABI-2 signal drives real PPU pixels: this drives real dots through a
frame, switches the background map at LY=3 the way Ghost Babel's HUD band
does, and checks what each row recorded. It also proves the record is the
frame's, not the session's - a frame that does not switch re-records every
row.
---
