From 4c449ecec8bdee12f1463512c17b794e256efb28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <moises.santana@ifba.edu.br>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:17:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 24/36] audio: let the host choose the mastering default

The mastering chain has always defaulted to off, which makes the remaster artifact's mastered-audio claim depend on the player finding a checkbox. The default is now a host choice: gb_platform_set_audio_mastering_default() is read by set_default_audio_preferences(), and the remaster host sets it before gb_platform_init.

A saved audio.mastering preference in runtime_prefs.ini still wins, so a player who chose raw audio keeps that choice across launches. gb_platform_get_audio_mastering() exposes the effective state for the performance report.
